# Frame budget over a whole rescue trip (the busiest moments: 16 people
# boarding, 16 more running into the hangar).
# A whole trip: fly to the nearest barracks, land, shoot it open, take 16
# people aboard, fly home, land on the pad, they run into the hangar.
wait-serial "AGK t0" 1000
press fire 2
wait 125
press up 30
press left 170
wait 60
press down 70
expect-serial "landed x=2334"
press fire 1
wait 25
press fire 1
wait 30
expect-serial "barracks open=3"
wait 90
wait 200
expect-serial "aboard=16"
press up 30
press right 180
wait 50
press down 70
expect-serial "landed x=2910"
wait 200
wait 120
expect-serial "saved=16"
expect-serial "trip=1"
expect-no-serial "chopper lost"
expect-no-dropped-frames
# (80 until the tank tell, quarter-pixel scroll, dithered sky, preview card
# and hall of fame: the heaviest picture - 16 people running into the hangar
# while the score bar types - went 79% -> 81%, about 1% of it the dithered
# sky's copper DMA, the rest spread thin; still ~19% short of a dropped frame.
# The deep rotor and jet fairness took it to 85%; the perf trim brought it to
# 80%: erases in the top border beside the HUD typing, fewer DIVUs for the
# HUD's numbers, the pacing sample off the status line's frames)
expect-max-load 83
expect-min-chip-free 64
